  "versionRationale": "1.3.0: training-export allows an empty provenance list only when includedCount is 0, and rejects includedCount >= 1 without layerStackDigests or snapshotRefs. 1.2.0 (P4.6, owner Q1=a): usage.prepared_disclosure gains a closed kind=navigation variant for exact revision/unit Usage without a fabricated search Selection. The old chunk payload and all existing valid/invalid vectors remain unchanged; navigation-specific closed-payload, tenant binding, empty-unit, immutable SQL identity and replay negatives are exercised in tests/reading/navigation/ProtocolTest.php and the reading:navigation manifest. This updates only the changed domain-event schema digest. 1.1.0 (P1.4 correction round 2): 29 bundled schemas (new job record), 187-entry corpus, 67 hash, 21 locator and 14 binding vectors. New required cases: contract.selection-run-binding (Selection keeps the trusted runRef; other run, dropped run and run-on-direct-call are denied, direct call stays allowed), contract.event-payload-closed (one closed payload per event type; documentText, credentials and unknown members rejected with a correct payloadDigest), contract.evidence-revision-identity (one documentRevisionId never names two irDigests; the corpus fixtures were corrected), contract.error-code-case (POLICY_CHANGED, RETRYABLE_LOCK_TIMEOUT, POINTER_CONFLICT, HOLD_TOO_LATE keep their case) and contract.job-record (five job states, lease fields, decimal fence). Golden digests that changed (domain-event payload, evidence-set, binding vectors) changed because the contract changed, see the corpus versionRationale. 1.0.0: initial P1.4 version; golden digests cross-checked with the independent rfc8785 package and schema-stage outcomes with python-jsonschema 2020-12 (tests/contract/schemas/evidence/independent-verification.json). Any change to a schema, vector or expected outcome requires a new fixtureVersion with a substantive rationale, never a mechanical snapshot rewrite.",
